 * `zainactive-rolls-ideal-applications.jpg` — NOT present in the repo. The
 * proven hub asset `dubai-high-rise-gym-rubber-rolls.webp` (1408×768, already
 * used on src/pages/gym-flooring-rolls.astro) is used in its place so the page
 * renders without a broken image. TODO: swap in the dedicated asset when
 * supplied, and convert the three new JPEGs to optimised WebP to match the
 * zainsquare / hub asset pipeline. og:image falls back to the hero file (no
 * purpose-built 1200×630 card yet).
 *
 * ─── DECISIONS TAKEN ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 *   - Hero "Request Free Material" CTA scrolls to the in-page lead-capture form
 *     (id="lead-form", Section 10) — a Netlify Forms POST, matching the zero-JS
 *     pattern in src/pages/contact.astro and the zainduo sibling. The secondary
 *     button opens WhatsApp.
 *   - Palette: the build request described a "dark / neutral-950 / emerald-600
 *     WhatsApp" system. That does NOT match this project — the live site and
 *     every sibling spoke (zainduo, zainsquare, zainfit) use the light
 *     industrial system from CLAUDE.md (charcoal text, industrial-100 sections,
 *     white cards, amber-400 primary CTA, charcoal/white ghost secondary).
 *     This page follows the established system for design-system consistency;
 *     the emerald WhatsApp accent is intentionally not used.
 *   - Structured data: a single combined @graph (BreadcrumbList + Product +
 *     FAQPage) emitted inline, matching zainduo. The visible breadcrumb trail is
 *     hand-rolled (not <Breadcrumbs />) so the BreadcrumbList is declared
 *     exactly once. Organization JSON-LD is still emitted sitewide by BaseLayout.
 *   - Canonical host: the request shows "rukanalzain.com"; the configured site
 *     is "ruknalzain.ae" (astro.config.mjs) — canonical is built from that
